==English==

===Etymology===
{{der|en|la|admixtūra}}, from {{m|la|admixtus}}, past participle of {{m|la|admisceō||to mix in}}, from {{m|la|misceō||to mix}}. Analyzable as {{pre|en|ad|mixture}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ədˈmɪkst͡ʃɚ/|/ædˈmɪkst͡ʃɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-admixture.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An instance of [[admix]]ing, a mixing in of something.
#: {{ux|en|The '''admixture''' of vanilla extract in the dough improved the pastries' flavor.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=March|author=J. H. Lehmann, A. D. Johnson, W. C. Bridges, J. Michel, D. M. Green|title=Cardiac Catheterization—A Diagnostic Aid in Congenital Heart Disease|journal=Northwest Medicine|volume=50|issue=3|location=Portland, Ore.|publisher=Northwest Medical Publishing Association|page=170|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/northwestmedicin5019nort/page/170/mode/2up?q=admixture|passage=Gas analysis of blood samples, obtained from different sites in the heart and great vessels, permits demonstration of '''admixture''' of oxygenated blood in the venous side or '''admixture''' of venous blood in the arterial side of the circulation.}}
## A mixing-in of a biologically or genetically differentiated group to an established stock.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1883|author=[[w:Robert Louis Stevenson|Robert Louis Stevenson]]|title=[[w:Treasure Island|Treasure Island]]|passage={{...}} the wood still flourished high and dense, all of fir on the land side, but towards the sea with a large '''admixture''' of live oaks.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|title=The Curse of Yig|author=H. P. Lovecraft and Zealia Bishop|passage=Both were lean, raw-boned specimens; the man tall, sandy, and grey-eyed, and the woman short and rather dark, with a black straightness of hair suggesting a slight Indian '''admixture'''.}}
# A [[mixture]], {{n-g|in some contexts:}}
## {{lb|en|epilepsy}} a mixture composed of entities retaining their individual properties.
##: ''Background EEG demonstrates an '''admixture''' of theta and delta waves.''

